-- `number` is not a Saule type. It existed only as an internal sentinel in
-- the native signature registry meaning "integer or float accepted", and it
-- never worked the other way: a `number` value was assignable to neither
-- `integer` nor `float`, so anything annotated with it was unusable.
--
-- Rejecting it has to cover every position a type can be written — this
-- fixture pins the binding one; the checker also rejects it on parameters,
-- return types, table element types, class fields and `as` targets.

local n: number = 5
println(n)
